  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>For the given reaction, if the initial pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmHg</mi></math> and the pressure at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>720</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mmHg</mi></math> at a constant temperature<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and constant volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The fraction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> decomposed under these conditions is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (nearest integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
